  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#42401\", \"PowerToys#42984\", \"PowerToys#45960\"], \"answer\": \"Other users have already asked for this. Light Switch has no option to change the wallpaper, or start a slideshow from a chosen folder, when the theme switches. PowerToys#42401 is the main request. The maintainers closed #42984, which asks for separate light and dark slideshow folders, as a duplicate of it. #45960 asks for one wallpaper per mode. Add your use case, including the folder-per-theme idea, to #42401 and give it a thumbs-up. Until the feature exists, you can use a separate tool such as Auto Dark Mode. You can also use a script or scheduled task that sets the wallpaper at sunrise and sunset. PowerToys#46722 asks for Light Switch to run custom commands on a mode change, and that would also cover this.\"}",
